\pard\hyphpar0\sb15\sa15\fi0\li0\ri0\ql\fs18{\f0 An analysis not specified in the protocol, treating the CIBIC+ score as a categorical rather than a continuous variable.\line The seven categories are the CIBIC+ scale as the study's statistical analysis plan defines it (Appendix 1, section 14.1.2): 1 = marked improvement through 7 = marked worsening, with 4 = no change. Every category is reported at every visit, including those no subject was scored in.\line Values are last observation carried forward within the analysis window (ADQSCIBC ANL01FL = 'Y').\line Column headings are the size of the efficacy analysis set; n is the number of subjects with a value at the visit, and percentages are of that n.\line The p-value is an overall comparison of the three treatment groups by the Cochran-Mantel-Haenszel row-mean-scores statistic on 2 degrees of freedom, stratified by site group. It is a single test per visit, printed once.}\cell
